      <item>
    <title>Global Burden of Disease Study 2023 (GBD 2023) Human Resources for Health Estimates 1990-2023</title>
    <link>https://ghdx.healthdata.org/record/ihme-data/global-human-resources-for-health-estimates-1990-2023</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-time field-type-datetime field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;January, 1990 - December, 2023&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;	&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-type field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
				&lt;div class=&quot;field-items clearfix&quot;&gt;
							&lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/data-type/estimate&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Estimate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
					&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-provider field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-inline clearfix&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Provider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/organizations/institute-health-metrics-and-evaluation-ihme&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-summary field-type-text field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Global Burden of Disease Study 2023 (GBD 2023), coordinated by the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME), estimated the burden of diseases, injuries, and risk factors for 204 countries and territories and selected subnational location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This dataset provides estimates of the density (per 10,000) and sex composition of 20 human resources for health cadres. Input data was drawn from population-based surveys, censuses, administrative records, and scientific literature harmonized to the International Standard Classification of Occupations 2008. Minimum density thresholds for doctors, nurses and midwives, dentists, and pharmacists associated with reaching a score of 80 out of 100 on the UHC effective coverage index are included. Estimates were generated using spatiotemporal Gaussian process regression(ST-GPR) models, and stochastic frontier meta-regression was used to derive minimum density thresholds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
     <pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:13:03 -0700</pubDate>
 <dc:creator>GHDx</dc:creator>
 <guid isPermaLink="false">631426 at https://ghdx.healthdata.org</guid>
 <comments />
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Honduras Regional Malaria Elimination Initiative Baseline Household Survey 2020</title>
    <link>https://ghdx.healthdata.org/record/ihme-data/HND-RMEI-2020</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-time field-type-datetime field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;January, 2018 - December, 2020&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-secondary field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items clearfix&quot;&gt;
		&lt;div class=&quot;field-item&quot;&gt;
						&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/data-type/survey&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Survey&lt;/a&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;
						Health facility - Household - Individual		&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-provider field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-inline clearfix&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Provider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/organizations/institute-health-metrics-and-evaluation-ihme&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-summary field-type-text field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Regional Malaria Elimination Initiative (RMEI), run by the Inter-American Development Bank, targets zero malaria cases across nine Mesoamerican/Caribbean countries, including Guatemala, Colombia, and the Dominican Republic. IHME was its independent evaluator. RMEI&#039;s baseline measurement tracks indicators along the &quot;Detection, Diagnosis, Treatment, Investigation, Response (DTI-R)&quot; strategy: input supply, testing rates, timeliness of detection/treatment, reporting quality, and vector control coverage. IHME built survey instruments from the indicator manual and a Guatemala fact-finding visit, with Ministry of Health input. Measurement includes a facility survey (interview, observation, records review) and an LQAS household survey near selected facilities, covering primary care sites in malaria focus areas plus linked hospitals/headquarters (referral, diagnosis, surveillance pipelines), and a household survey gathering detection, prevention, and knowledge data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
     <pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:32:13 -0700</pubDate>
 <dc:creator>GHDx</dc:creator>
 <guid isPermaLink="false">630112 at https://ghdx.healthdata.org</guid>
 <comments />
  </item>
