  <item>
    <title>Global Burden of Disease Study 2023 (GBD 2023) Morbidity Gap Estimates 1990-2023</title>
    <link>https://ghdx.healthdata.org/record/ihme-data/gbd-2023-morbidity-gap-1990-2023</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-time field-type-datetime field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;January, 1990 - December, 2023&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;	&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-type field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
				&lt;div class=&quot;field-items clearfix&quot;&gt;
							&lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/data-type/estimate&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Estimate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
					&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-provider field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-inline clearfix&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Provider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/organizations/institute-health-metrics-and-evaluation-ihme&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-summary field-type-text field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Global Burden of Disease Study 2023 (GBD 2023), coordinated by the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME), estimated life expectancy (LE) and healthy life expectancy (HALE) at birth for 204 countries and territories and selected subnational locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This dataset includes selected appendix tables as well as estimates of the morbidity gap (MG), defined as the duration of life spent in poor health, calculated as LE minus HALE, and the proportional MG, defined as the proportion of life spent in poor health, calculated as MG/LE*100%. Estimates were produced globally and for GBD super-regions, countries and territories, and Socio-demographic Index (SDI) quintiles; for the years 1990, 2010, and 2020–2023 for the MG and for the years 1990 and 2023 for the proportional MG; and for males, females, and all sexes combined.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
     <pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 09:16:42 -0700</pubDate>
 <dc:creator>GHDx</dc:creator>
 <guid isPermaLink="false">629003 at https://ghdx.healthdata.org</guid>
 <comments />
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Hemoglobin Concentration Effects on Maternal Peripartum Depression Burden of Proof and Risk-Outcome Scores</title>
    <link>https://ghdx.healthdata.org/record/ihme-data/hemoglobin-maternal-ppd-bop-ros</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-time field-type-datetime field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;July, 2026 - July, 2026&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;	&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-type field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
				&lt;div class=&quot;field-items clearfix&quot;&gt;
							&lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/data-type/estimate&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Estimate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
					&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-provider field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-inline clearfix&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Provider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/organizations/institute-health-metrics-and-evaluation-ihme&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-summary field-type-text field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Researchers systematically reviewed literature on the health burden of low and high hemoglobin concentrations during pregnancy. Utilizing the Burden of Proof (BoP) methodology, estimates were created to summarize the relationship between maternal hemoglobin levels and peripartum depression. A sensitivity analysis restricted to observations with postnatal depression as outcome was also performed. The datasets include 1) input data to BoP analysis and 2) its outputs including the pooled relative risks as well as metrics like burden of proof risk function, risk-outcome score, and star rating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
     <pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:49:18 -0700</pubDate>
 <dc:creator>GHDx</dc:creator>
 <guid isPermaLink="false">627764 at https://ghdx.healthdata.org</guid>
 <comments />
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>United States Colorectal Cancer Mortality by County, Race and Ethnicity 2000-2019</title>
    <link>https://ghdx.healthdata.org/record/ihme-data/us-colorectal-cancer-county-race-ethnicity-2000-2019</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-time field-type-datetime field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;January, 2000 - December, 2019&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;	&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-type field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
				&lt;div class=&quot;field-items clearfix&quot;&gt;
							&lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/data-type/estimate&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Estimate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
					&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-provider field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-inline clearfix&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Provider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/organizations/institute-health-metrics-and-evaluation-ihme&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-summary field-type-text field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Estimates of Colorectal Cancer mortality rates were produced at the county level in the United States, and by racial and ethnic population, for 2000-2019. They were generated using data from the National Center for Health Statistics. For age groups outside the range estimated for colorectal cancer under GBD age restrictions, rates are reported as zero. Estimates for population groups too small to produce stable rates were masked and appear as empty cells.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This data set includes the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CSV files of county-, state-, and national-level estimates of Colorectal Cancer mortality rates for each age group, sex, year, and racial and ethnic population (non-Latino and non-Hispanic American Indian or Alaska Native [AIAN], non-Latino and non-Hispanic Asian or Pacific Islander [Asian], non-Latino and non-Hispanic Black [Black], Latino or Hispanic [Latino], and non-Latino and non-Hispanic White [White]). Blank cells are for masked estimates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code used to generate the estimates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
     <pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:13:44 -0700</pubDate>
 <dc:creator>GHDx</dc:creator>
 <guid isPermaLink="false">626511 at https://ghdx.healthdata.org</guid>
 <comments />
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Hemoglobin Concentration Effects on Maternal and Neonatal Health Burden of Proof and Risk-Outcome Scores</title>
    <link>https://ghdx.healthdata.org/record/ihme-data/hemoglobin-maternal-neonatal-bop-ros</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-time field-type-datetime field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;June, 2026 - June, 2026&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;	&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-type field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
				&lt;div class=&quot;field-items clearfix&quot;&gt;
							&lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/data-type/estimate&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Estimate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
					&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-provider field-type-taxonomy-term-reference field-label-inline clearfix&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Provider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/organizations/institute-health-metrics-and-evaluation-ihme&quot; typeof=&quot;skos:Concept&quot; property=&quot;rdfs:label skos:prefLabel&quot; datatype=&quot;&quot;&gt;Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-name-field-summary field-type-text field-label-hidden&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
          &lt;div class=&quot;field-item even&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Researchers systematically reviewed literature on the health burden of low and high hemoglobin concentrations during pregnancy. Utilizing the Burden of Proof (BoP) methodology, estimates were created to summarize the relationship between maternal hemoglobin levels and 13 adverse maternal and neonatal outcomes, including all-cause maternal mortality, postpartum hemorrhage, antepartum hemorrhage, preeclampsia, maternal sepsis and other infections, peripartum depression, all-cause neonatal mortality, all-cause stillbirth, preterm birth, low birthweight, small-for-gestational-age, large-for-gestational-age, and neonatal sepsis. Various sensitivity analyses based on the trimester-specific hemoglobin assessments and different definitions of outcomes, amongst others, were also performed. The datasets include 1) input data to BoP analysis and 2) its outputs including the pooled relative risks as well as metrics like burden of proof risk function, risk-outcome score, and star rating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description>
     <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 09:19:27 -0700</pubDate>
 <dc:creator>GHDx</dc:creator>
